# THE SWEEP — the generic weirdness hunt, replayable on any surface/offering pair.
#
#   cargo run -p dregg-drive -- --surface web --offering tug --as alice \
#       --state-dir /tmp/sweep-tug-web --script dregg-drive/scripts/sweep.drive
#
# Every line here is one of the failure classes a single-step render test cannot reach.
# `#` comments and blank lines are skipped, so this file IS the transcript language.

# ── 1. the first look, and the SECOND look ──────────────────────────────────
# A second request is where the re-present bug lives: on a chat surface an EDIT to a
# message that has scrolled away is indistinguishable from a dead bot.
open
again

# ── 2. play ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
press 0
again
press 0

# ── 3. FOG — switch who is looking, nothing else. `as` re-requests and diffs
#        the CONTROL LABELS, because a leak has hidden in a button while the
#        prose sections were correct.
as bob
press 0
as alice

# ── 4. the chain still re-verifies through the surface's own verify path ────
verify

# ── 5. ⚑ RESTART — rebuild the host from the durable store, mid-session. The
#        messages/tab the user is looking at do NOT vanish; the bot's memory of
#        them does. Then press what is still on their screen.
restart
stale 0
press 0
verify

# ── 6. WRONG INPUT — a refusal that is illegible is a defect, and the only way
#        to find that out is to try. Out-of-range index, a verb from no phase,
#        an unknown command.
press 99
act nonsense 999
act press -1
send /help
send hello are you alive

# ── 7. where we ended up ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
again
controls
